@baseUrl = https://localhost:7164
@cityId = 2
@pointOfInterestId = 3

### No token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities
Accept: application/json

### Log in and get a JWT
# @name tokenRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authentication/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Sengul",
  "password": "demo"
}

### -----------------------------------------------------
### 0. REGISTER & LOGIN
### -----------------------------------------------------

### Register: geldige user → 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authentication/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Sengul",
  "firstName": "Sengül",
  "lastName": "Karakaya",
  "password": "DemoPassword1"
}

### Register: zelfde naam met hoofdletters → verwacht 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authentication/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "SENGUL",
  "firstName": "Sengül",
  "lastName": "Karakaya",
  "password": "DemoPassword1"
}

### Register: wachtwoord te kort → verwacht 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authentication/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "testuser",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "password": "12345"
}

### Login: geldige user → 200 + token
# @name loginRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authentication/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "sengul",
  "password": "DemoPassword1"
}

### Login: fout wachtwoord → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authentication/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Sengul",
  "password": "FoutWachtwoord1"
}

### Login: onbestaande user → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authentication/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "bestaatniet",
  "password": "DemoPassword1"
}

### Steden ophalen met de echte token → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRequest.response.body.$.token}}


### -----------------------------------------------------
### 1. CITIES 
### -----------------------------------------------------

### All cities, with token -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

### Filter by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities?name=Antwerp
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

### Search in name and description
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities?searchQuery=park
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

### Paging (check the X-Pagination response header)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities?pageNumber=1&pageSize=2
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

### One city with its points of interest
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities/{{cityId}}?includePointsOfInterest=false
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

### City that doesn't exist -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities/999
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

### XML instead of JSON (content negotiation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities
Accept: application/xml
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}


### -----------------------------------------------------
### 2. VERSIONING
### -----------------------------------------------------

### Points of interest in v1 -> 404 (only exists in v2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

### Points of interest in v2 -> 200 (check api-supported-versions header)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}


### -----------------------------------------------------
### 3. POINTS OF INTEREST (v2)
### -----------------------------------------------------

### Create -> 201 Created + Location header
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "MAS",
  "description": "Museum on the river, with a free view over the city."
}

### Create with invalid data (no name) -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "description": "No name, so validation fails."
}

### Full update (PUT) -> 204
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest/{{pointOfInterestId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Cathedral of Our Lady",
  "description": "Gothic cathedral in the centre of Antwerp."
}

### Partial update (PATCH, JSON Patch) -> 204
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest/{{pointOfInterestId}}
Content-Type: application/json-patch+json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

[
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/description",
    "value": "Only the description was changed."
  }
]

### PATCH that removes the name -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest/{{pointOfInterestId}}
Content-Type: application/json-patch+json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

[
  {
    "op": "remove",
    "path": "/name"
  }
]

### Bulk update of all descriptions (one SQL UPDATE)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest/bulk
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "newDescription": "Description set by a bulk update."
}

### Delete -> 204 (check the console for the "mail")
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/cities/{{cityId}}/pointsofinterest/{{pointOfInterestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}


### -----------------------------------------------------
### 4. FILES
### -----------------------------------------------------

### Download (v0.1, deprecated -> check api-deprecated-versions header)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v0.1/files/any-id
Accept: application/pdf
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}

### Upload a PDF
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRequest.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----CityInfoBoundary

------CityInfoBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample-file.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample-file.pdf
------CityInfoBoundary--


### -----------------------------------------------------
### 5. OPENAPI DOCUMENTS
### (Scalar UI in the browser: https://localhost:7164/scalar)
### -----------------------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v2.json
Accept: application/json
